Production Safety Checklist
- [ ] Use IAM roles, profiles, or OIDC rather than hardcoded
  credentials.
- [ ] Start with read-only permissions.
- [ ] Specify the intended AWS account and region.
- [ ] Handle pagination and API exceptions.
- [ ] Set sensible timeouts and retry behavior.
- [ ] Add unit tests with mocked AWS clients.
- [ ] Scan code and dependencies for security issues.
- [ ] Require approval for destructive or production-changing actions.
- [ ] Keep secrets, sensitive output, and private infrastructure
  details out of Git.
